  "prompt": "Find the common rule that maps an input grid to an output grid, given the examples below. Generate a python script that takes a grid as input and transforms it according to the this rule. Anticipate that this program will be applied to several grids, not only the shown test grid.\n\nYour script must define exactly one callable entrypoint:\ndef solve(grid):\nwhere `grid` is passed as a list of lists of integers (list[list[int]]) and the function returns the transformed grid in the same format.\n\nExample 1:\n\nInput:\n4 5 4\n5 5 5\n4 5 4\nOutput:\n0 4 0\n4 4 4\n0 4 0\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput:\n5 5 6 6 6\n6 5 5 6 6\n6 6 5 5 6\n6 6 6 5 5\n5 6 6 6 5\nOutput:\n6 6 0 0 0\n0 6 6 0 0\n0 0 6 6 0\n0 0 0 6 6\n6 0 0 0 6\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput:\n9 5 9 9 9\n9 9 5 5 9\n9 5 9 9 9\n9 9 5 9 9\n9 9 9 5 5\nOutput:\n0 9 0 0 0\n0 0 9 9 0\n0 9 0 0 0\n0 0 9 0 0\n0 0 0 9 9\n\nBelow is a test input grid.\n\nInput:\n3 3 3 5 3\n3 5 3 3 3\n3 5 5 3 5\n3 3 3 5 3\n5 5 5 3 3\n\nYour final answer should just be the python script itself, no other text or markdown.",
  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return grid\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    from collections import Counter\n    border_counts = Counter()\n    \n    for i in range(rows):\n        for j in range(cols):\n            if i == 0 or i == rows - 1 or j == 0 or j == cols - 1:\n                border_counts[grid[i][j]] += 1\n    \n    # Find the value that appears most on the border; tie -> smaller value\n    max_count = max(border_counts.values())\n    selected = min(val for val, cnt in border_counts.items() if cnt == max_count)\n    \n    # Transform: selected -> 0, everything else -> selected\n    result = [[0 if cell == selected else selected for cell in row] for row in grid]\n    return result",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return grid\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    from collections import Counter\n    border_counts = Counter()\n    \n    for i in range(rows):\n        for j in range(cols):\n            if i == 0 or i == rows - 1 or j == 0 or j == cols - 1:\n                border_counts[grid[i][j]] += 1\n    \n    # Find the value that appears most on the border; tie -> smaller value\n    max_count = max(border_counts.values())\n    selected = min(val for val, cnt in border_counts.items() if cnt == max_count)\n    \n    # Transform: selected -> 0, everything else -> selected\n    result = [[0 if cell == selected else selected for cell in row] for row in grid]\n    return result",
